/-!
# Almost-linear approximation of edit distance

A uniform binary randomized approximation scheme attains success probability
at least two thirds, returns zero on equal strings, uses almost-linear expected
work for each fixed binary accuracy, and has polynomial space on every outcome.
Finite Bernstein concentration discharges the hypotheses of its conditional
accuracy and work bounds.
-/
